You are tasked with updating the frontend application to implement key user-facing functionality by integrating with the existing backend APIs. The backend already handles all business logic and data operations. Your responsibility is to build or update the frontend to interface cleanly with the backend and provide a complete, visual, and user-friendly experience.

⚠️ Important Constraints:

Do not modify the backend code. All logic must use existing backend functionality.

You must not replicate business logic in the frontend — only call APIs and display/submit data.

Ensure that unit tests cover the new frontend components and functionality.

Reuse or update existing code where needed as opposed to creating duplicate code.

KEEP THE IMPLEMENTATION, AND TESTS, DRY!!!

🔍 Step 1: Backend Audit

Begin by reviewing the backend codebase (or available documentation) to identify existing endpoints related to:

Program creation and preferences

Workout generation and history

User profile, statistics, and performance data

1RM tracking and estimation

Exercise history and rotation

Map out what backend operations are already available and how they align with the feature requirements below.

🧩 Frontend Feature Requirements
User Profile Page

Dashboard Display:

